const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"用中国经验追问跨国规律的边界",en:"Use China to question the boundaries of cross-country regularities"},body:{zh:"Allen、Qian与Qian将中国当时的增长经验与法律、金融和增长文献对照，提醒跨国平均关系可能遗漏大型经济体内部的差异。问题不是简单选边支持或反对法律保护，而是现有解释能否覆盖不同部门的融资与治理方式。",en:"Allen, Qian and Qian compare China's historical growth with law-and-finance research, questioning whether country averages obscure internal differences. The issue is not a simple vote for or against legal protection, but whether existing explanations cover different financing and governance arrangements."},reference:{url:"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/11-946-planning-in-transition-economies-for-growth-and-equity-spring-2004/9257eee0807f159387f0a70050eb3359_feb_17.pdf",label:{zh:"2004年2月3日修订稿 · §I · pp. 1–2",en:"February 3, 2004 revision · §I · pp. 1–2"}}},{title:{zh:"先按论文定义理解三个部门",en:"Read the three sectors using the paper's definitions"},body:{zh:"工作稿分别讨论国有、上市及其定义下的Private Sector。最后一类包含其他私人和部分地方政府相关所有制，不能直接翻译成今天统计口径下的纯民营企业。部门比较之前，应保留作者的分类，避免把不同年代的名称当作完全一致。",en:"The draft discusses state, listed and its defined Private Sector, the last including private and some local-government-related ownership. It is not identical to a present-day purely private-firm category. Preserve the authors' definitions before comparing sectors across periods."},reference:{url:"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/11-946-planning-in-transition-economies-for-growth-and-equity-spring-2004/9257eee0807f159387f0a70050eb3359_feb_17.pdf",label:{zh:"2004年2月3日修订稿 · §I · p. 2; footnote 6",en:"February 3, 2004 revision · §I · p. 2; footnote 6"}}},{title:{zh:"上市公司不能代表全部企业融资",en:"Listed companies do not represent all corporate finance"},body:{zh:"作者把上市公司样本与其他部门分开，指出公开证券市场只是企业融资的一部分。对上市公司分红、估值或股权集中度的观察，不能自动说明非上市企业怎样取得资金。只用股票数据库研究整体经济，会遗漏另一种重要的样本选择。",en:"The article separates listed-company evidence from other sectors because public securities are only one financing channel. Listed-company dividends, valuations and ownership do not explain how all unlisted firms obtain funds. A stock database introduces a consequential selection boundary."},reference:{url:"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/11-946-planning-in-transition-economies-for-growth-and-equity-spring-2004/9257eee0807f159387f0a70050eb3359_feb_17.pdf",label:{zh:"2004年2月3日修订稿 · §I · pp. 3–4",en:"February 3, 2004 revision · §I · pp. 3–4"}}},{title:{zh:"访谈提供机制线索，不是全国估计",en:"Interviews provide mechanism evidence, not national estimates"},body:{zh:"这一早期稿的私人部门证据主要来自浙江与江苏17位创业者和管理者的访谈，地区本身也较发达。它能帮助理解亲友、金融机构和关系网络的作用，但不能据此计算全国企业使用某融资渠道的精确比例，更不能混用后续版本样本。",en:"This early draft relies mainly on interviews with 17 entrepreneurs and executives in Zhejiang and Jiangsu. These developed regions offer mechanism evidence about family, institutions and relationships, not a precise national financing share. Later-version samples must not be substituted silently."},reference:{url:"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/11-946-planning-in-transition-economies-for-growth-and-equity-spring-2004/9257eee0807f159387f0a70050eb3359_feb_17.pdf",label:{zh:"2004年2月3日修订稿 · §I · p. 4",en:"February 3, 2004 revision · §I · p. 4"}}},{title:{zh:"声誉与重复合作可以影响履约",en:"Reputation and repeated relationships can affect enforcement"},body:{zh:"工作稿讨论声誉、关系、竞争和共享未来收益如何约束参与者行为。这些机制依赖持续合作的价值与具体环境，并不是无成本、无风险的正式制度替代物。看到某些企业通过关系融资成功，也不能推断所有企业都能获得同样机会。",en:"The draft discusses reputation, relationships, competition and shared future gains as constraints on behavior. These mechanisms depend on continued cooperation and context; they are not costless substitutes for formal institutions. Success among some firms does not imply equal access for all."},reference:{url:"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/11-946-planning-in-transition-economies-for-growth-and-equity-spring-2004/9257eee0807f159387f0a70050eb3359_feb_17.pdf",label:{zh:"2004年2月3日修订稿 · §I · pp. 4–5",en:"February 3, 2004 revision · §I · pp. 4–5"}}},{title:{zh:"比较解释，不把历史研究变成今日制度结论",en:"Compare explanations without turning history into a current institutional claim"},body:{zh:"这篇研究提供的是特定转型时期的部门比较与机制讨论。与投资者保护文献并读时，应区分外部公开融资、关系型融资和企业增长这几个结果。历史上存在替代渠道，不等于正式保护不重要，也不证明今天的法律和融资条件仍与当时相同。",en:"This is a sector comparison from a particular transition period. Read it alongside investor-protection research while separating public external finance, relationship finance and growth. Alternative channels do not make formal protection irrelevant or establish that today's institutions match the historical setting."},reference:{url:"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/11-946-planning-in-transition-economies-for-growth-and-equity-spring-2004/9257eee0807f159387f0a70050eb3359_feb_17.pdf",label:{zh:"2004年2月3日修订稿 · §I",en:"February 3, 2004 revision · §I"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"导读依据2004年工作稿，不能当作当前中国制度或融资结构的说明。稿中的Private Sector包括部分地方政府相关所有制，访谈证据也不代表全国随机样本。",en:"The 2004 draft is not a description of current Chinese institutions or financing. Its Private Sector includes some local-government-related ownership, and its interviews are not a national random sample."}};export{e as default};
